# Source templates

- Read `src-templates/AI-INSTRUCTIONS.md` and the nearest project `AI-INSTRUCTIONS.md`.
- Treat scaffolds as templates, not production apps—avoid inventing real connection strings or secrets.
- Keep SourceMonolith domain project boundaries intact.
- EF migrations belong in dedicated `*.Migrations` projects; do not mix with SQL `.sqlproj` ownership of the same objects.
- Prefer BuildingBlocks abstractions over duplicating data-access or observability code.
- Update matching test project READMEs/instructions when contracts or layering rules change.
- For DbIntelligence local ops, prefer `scripts/*.ps1` and user-scoped Node via `Initialize-DbIntelligenceNode.ps1` (fnm, no admin). Prefer Codegraph via `fnm exec --using=lts-latest -- npm i -g @colbymchenry/codegraph` when fnm is present.
